Spec: Authenticated transport control authority

Platform: Go `1.27`

Purpose:
  Authorize individually authenticated devices and exact published services before transport admission.

Owns:
  ./go.mod
  ./go.sum
  ./README.md

Structure:
  ./authority: Durable roles, services, grants and standard short-lived leases.
  ./serverhost: Protected Linux identity and durable authority lifecycle for explicit server commands.
  ./controlinterop: Independent real mTLS control verification fixture.
  ./interop: Local public fixture issuer for independent .NET/Java verification.

References:
  /docs/SECURITY-SPEC.md
  /docs/adr/0015-authenticated-transport-control.md

Must:
  Keep new control authority separate from the legacy shared-token deployment.
  Use mature TLS, JWS and transactional storage; never place device keys or backend credentials in application SDKs.
  Treat actual backend admission and active direct/relay revocation as release gates, not inferred consequences of library tests.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify durable device/service authority and standard scoped lease enforcement.
  [x] #2 Bind real mTLS control identity to FRP backend admission and active sessions.
